10.2 The Contractor shall, within twenty-eight (28) days of becoming aware, or of when it ought reasonably to have become aware, of any event or circumstance which is or may be a ground for an extension of time, give written notice to the Employer's Representative of such event or circumstance, with full particulars. The Contractor shall also keep such contemporary records as may reasonably be necessary to substantiate the claim.

10.3 Within forty-two (42) days of the end of the month in which the event or circumstance occurred, or within such other period as the Employer's Representative may agree in writing, the Contractor shall submit a fully detailed claim for extension of time, including:

(a) a description of the event or circumstance;

(b) the date on which the event or circumstance commenced and, if continuing, the date on which it ceased or is expected to cease;

(c) a detailed analysis of the delay caused by the event or circumstance, including the effect on the critical path of the Works;

(d) the period of extension of time claimed, together with supporting records and computations.

