10.4 The Employer's Representative shall, within twenty-eight (28) days of receipt of a fully detailed claim, or within such other period as may be agreed, assess the claim and notify the Contractor in writing of the extension of time, if any, which is granted, stating the reasons for the decision. If the Employer's Representative fails to respond within the stated period, the claim shall be deemed to have been rejected.

10.5 The Contractor shall continue to proceed with the Works and shall not suspend or slow down the Works pending the assessment of any claim for extension of time, except to the extent permitted by Clause 11 or by any other provision of the Contract.

10.6 No extension of time shall be granted for delay caused by the Contractor's own negligence, default, or failure to comply with its obligations under the Contract, or for delay which could reasonably have been avoided by the Contractor taking proper and timely measures.

**11.0 FORCE MAJEURE**

11.1 For the purposes of this Contract, "force majeure" means an exceptional event or circumstance:

(a) which is beyond a Party's control;

(b) which such Party could not reasonably have provided against before entering into the Contract;

(c) which, having arisen, such Party could not reasonably have avoided or overcome; and

(d) which is not substantially attributable to the other Party.

11.2 Force majeure may include, but is not limited to, the following events or circumstances, provided that they satisfy the conditions set out in Clause 11.1:

(a) war, hostilities, invasion, act of foreign enemy, or civil war;

(b) rebellion, terrorism, sabotage, riot, or military or usurped power;

**CONTRACT AGREEMENT FOR DREDGING WORKS**

**13.2** The Contractor shall deliver to the Employer, not less than fourteen (14) days before the Commencement Date, certificates or other satisfactory evidence of all insurances required under Clause 13.1. The Contractor shall not commence the Works until such certificates have been received and approved by the Employer.

**13.3** All insurances required under Clause 13.1 shall be effected with reputable insurers approved by the Employer, and shall include a waiver of subrogation in favour of the Employer and its officers, agents, and servants. The Contractor shall cause its insurers to give not less than thirty (30) days' written notice to the Employer prior to any cancellation, non-renewal, or material alteration of any such policy.

**13.4** If the Contractor fails to take out or maintain any insurance required under this Clause, the Employer may take out and maintain such insurance and may deduct the cost thereof from any monies due or to become due to the Contractor under the Contract.

**14.0 INDEMNITY**

**14.1** The Contractor shall indemnify and hold harmless the Employer, its officers, agents, and servants from and against all claims, demands, proceedings, costs, damages, and expenses whatsoever arising out of or in connection with:

(a) any injury to or death of any person, or damage to or loss of any property, caused by the negligence, breach of statutory duty, or other default of the Contractor, its Subcontractors, or their respective employees, agents, or invitees, in the performance of the Works;

(b) any infringement of any patent, trademark, copyright, or other intellectual property right arising from the use by the Contractor of any plant, equipment, material, or method in connection with the Works;

(c) any pollution or contamination of the waters, seabed, or foreshore of the Port caused by the Contractor's operations, save where such pollution or contamination results from the Employer's negligence or wilful default.

**14.2** The Contractor's liability under this Clause shall not be limited by reason of any insurance maintained pursuant to Clause 13, and the Contractor shall remain fully liable for any amounts not covered by such insurance.

**15.0 FORCE MAJEURE**

**15.1** Neither party shall be liable to the other for any failure or delay in performing its obligations under the Contract if such failure or delay is caused by a Force Majeure Event. For the purposes of this Contract, a Force Majeure Event means any event or circumstance beyond the reasonable control of the affected party, including but not limited to:

(a) acts of God, storm, flood, earthquake, or other natural disaster;

(b) war, hostilities, act of a public enemy, terrorism, or civil commotion;

(c) strike, lockout, or other industrial action, save where such action is caused by the affected party's own default;

(d) fire, explosion, or other accident;

(e) epidemic, pandemic, or other public health emergency;

(f) any law, regulation, order, or directive of any governmental or regulatory authority, including the Nigerian Ports Authority or the Federal Ministry of Transportation.

**15.2** The affected party shall give written notice to the other party of the occurrence of a Force Majeure Event within seven (7) days of its onset, stating the nature of the event, its expected duration, and the obligations affected thereby. The affected party shall use all reasonable endeavours to mitigate the effects of the Force Majeure Event and to resume performance of its obligations as soon as practicable.

**15.3** If a Force Majeure Event continues for a period exceeding sixty (60) consecutive days, either party may by written notice terminate the Contract. Upon such termination, the Contractor shall be entitled to payment for Works properly executed and for materials and plant delivered to the Site, less any advance payments outstanding, and shall remove its plant and equipment from the Site within thirty (30) days.
